WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.334
Hi, I'm Clementine!

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.073
Ming's design model draws interfaces.

00:00:04.073 --> 00:00:08.248
Its core is borrowed; what's new is how a prompt reaches it.

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:14.390
The idea: keep Z-Image's diffusion transformer, and swap the parts around it:

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:17.920
a new encoder, learned queries, and an alpha-channel decoder.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.063
The prompt goes into a Ming multimodal language model, with two hundred

00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:26.320
and fifty-six learnable query tokens appended.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.802
Those query states pass a Qwen connector, into the slot Z-Image's text

00:00:30.802 --> 00:00:32.156
encoder used to fill.

00:00:32.576 --> 00:00:36.794
In parallel, a shortcut takes layers five, twelve and twenty, and projects

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:38.903
them straight to the transformer's width.

00:00:39.323 --> 00:00:43.457
The transformer is Z-Image's base checkpoint, fine-tuned: the six billion in the

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:45.869
name, about a quarter of the download.

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:49.541
Its decoder is swapped for Qwen-Image-Layered's RGBA one.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:52.793
It fits because both use sixteen latent channels.

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.990
The Layer model asks the same body for frames.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.762
The first is the full composite.

00:00:59.182 --> 00:01:01.845
Then one RGBA layer per frame, front to back.

00:01:02.265 --> 00:01:04.913
The flat input joins as one more frame.

00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:08.223
Six layers means eight full frames, run twice per step.

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:10.209
Layer count is a latency dial.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.791
Here's the released six-layer example.

00:01:13.791 --> 00:01:15.533
A flat card goes in.

00:01:15.953 --> 00:01:20.330
Six RGBA layers come out: the text, two illustration layers, the ribbon,

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.153
the panel, the red background.

00:01:22.573 --> 00:01:24.187
Stacked, they recompose the card.

00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:27.650
What did the fine-tune buy?

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:32.291
A two-hundred-and-forty-four-point gain over its parent on design prompts: first of forty-two

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.224
open models, sixteenth of all.

00:01:35.433 --> 00:01:38.646
So the core is Z-Image's, re-aimed at a new encoder.

00:01:38.646 --> 00:01:40.894
The arena gain is what fine-tuning bought.

00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:47.702
To recap: a new encoder into Z-Image's transformer, an RGBA decoder,

00:01:47.702 --> 00:01:49.419
and layers as frames.

00:01:49.839 --> 00:01:52.097
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:52.097 --> 00:01:52.742
I'm Clementine.

00:01:52.742 --> 00:01:53.065
Bye!
